---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ToolCards from '@components/ToolCards.astro';
import Icon from '@components/Icon.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Tattoo tools - placement picker, size guide, quiz | TattooDesignsCo"
  description="Free tools to choose a tattoo placement, compare real sizes and get a shortlist in 30 seconds."
  path="/tools/"
  crumbs={[
    { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
    { label: 'Tools', href: '/tools/' },
  ]}
>
  <section class="container top">
    <h1>Tools</h1>
    <div class="lead">
      <p>Three small tools that answer the questions a gallery cannot.</p>
      <p>Everything runs in your browser - nothing is sent anywhere.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ToolCards />

  <section class="section container">
    <a class="panel panel-accent quiz" href="/tools/quiz/">
      <Icon name="timer" size={30} class="ic" />
      <div>
        <h2>30-second tattoo quiz</h2>
        <p class="small muted">
          Answer a few questions about placement, size and style, get a
          shortlist you can save.
        </p>
      </div>
      <Icon name="chevron" size={18} class="chev" />
    </a>
  </section>

  <section class="section container prose">
    <h2>Use the tools in this order</h2>
    <p>
      Start with placement if you already know the amount of visibility and
      coverage you want. The picker groups body areas by usable shape rather
      than presenting every tattoo as if it could be moved anywhere unchanged.
      A long forearm design, a shoulder cap and a small wrist symbol need
      different compositions.
    </p>
    <p>
      Open the size guide next and compare the reference images at a normal
      viewing distance. Three centimetres can hold a simple symbol, but not the
      same internal detail as a ten centimetre design. Use the measurement as a
      starting point for your artist, not as a fixed specification.
    </p>

    <h2>What the quiz does</h2>
    <p>
      The quiz is useful when you have not chosen a direction. It links each
      answer to a real placement, size or style page, so the result remains
      useful without an account. Save several references and note why each one
      works. The final shortlist should explain shape, scale and treatment
      rather than ask an artist to copy one image.
    </p>
    <p>
      Your saved list remains on the device you are using. Export or copy the
      final description before changing browsers or clearing site data. The
      tools do not submit a booking request and they do not send your choices to
      a studio.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .top { padding-top: 24px; }
  .top .lead { margin-top: 10px; }

  .quiz {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1fr auto;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 14px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .quiz:hover { color: inherit; }
  .ic, .chev { color: var(--accent); }
  h2 { font-size: 19px; margin-bottom: 4px; }
</style>
